[{:db/id 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c2de4bc9-44ca-5148-a12b-218413513154"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119653 :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](images/f9/f9fe9fa5e18e286ac7e026df2667c7a8ce259cd2c0416efe85d66d2546358dfd.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](images/9e/9e7b8bc888dbf7a764c0d5b9533758277b59e78d476a3cfe7bbfb2fcac7e7363.svg)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-072e9e45-d148-5a1a-9029-08725d744a80" "question-ee5f2c99-4524-5cc2-872a-3bdd6d04d82a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-152abe46-196c-57ed-801a-b01b3b6e9019"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c2de4bc9-44ca-5148-a12b-218413513154" :question/id #uuid "c2de4bc9-44ca-5148-a12b-218413513154" :question/math-academy-id "q-34071" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(1,1,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨3,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-8,4⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(3,0,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,0,1⟩-⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨1,-8,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-8)+2\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+8+8|}{\\sqrt{1+64+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|18|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1d64e0b6-2371-55aa-b403-0c4879d7c148"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1d64e0b6-2371-55aa-b403-0c4879d7c148" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d64e0b6-2371-55aa-b403-0c4879d7c148" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-da38d1c3-4b88-53eb-a80c-704d0e6c3e9d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da38d1c3-4b88-53eb-a80c-704d0e6c3e9d" "answer-466771cc-d368-518c-a407-118cef3850d5" "answer-63d845d3-365f-535b-afff-d5908b0a7da2" "answer-5cbe681d-c67b-512a-b210-fd917c390fd5" "answer-e59f1960-0256-5298-9dd6-cb0ef30a5ab8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da38d1c3-4b88-53eb-a80c-704d0e6c3e9d" :answer/id #uuid "da38d1c3-4b88-53eb-a80c-704d0e6c3e9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-466771cc-d368-518c-a407-118cef3850d5" :answer/id #uuid "466771cc-d368-518c-a407-118cef3850d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63d845d3-365f-535b-afff-d5908b0a7da2" :answer/id #uuid "63d845d3-365f-535b-afff-d5908b0a7da2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cbe681d-c67b-512a-b210-fd917c390fd5" :answer/id #uuid "5cbe681d-c67b-512a-b210-fd917c390fd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e59f1960-0256-5298-9dd6-cb0ef30a5ab8" :answer/id #uuid "e59f1960-0256-5298-9dd6-cb0ef30a5ab8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-072e9e45-d148-5a1a-9029-08725d744a80" :question/id #uuid "072e9e45-d148-5a1a-9029-08725d744a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-129126" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,4,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,1⟩=9.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,1⟩ & =9 \\\\ -3x+y+z & =9 \\\\ z & =9+3x-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+3(1)-(1)=11.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(1,1,11)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,11⟩-⟨-3,4,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-3,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-3+4|}{\\sqrt{9+1+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-11|}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-161dc5e7-caef-534f-b118-60aceff59caf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-161dc5e7-caef-534f-b118-60aceff59caf" :answer-field/id #uuid "161dc5e7-caef-534f-b118-60aceff59caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-088db5f4-36d3-5c78-98a0-f200bd4afcc7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a2a87c7-4871-52b2-9751-1dcf545d8473" "answer-9c4b18bd-d214-5ab3-980a-bcf8c20a44a8" "answer-a192f294-392f-523d-b854-34cf2ca91ca6" "answer-088db5f4-36d3-5c78-98a0-f200bd4afcc7" "answer-168db077-1d3d-5cb0-b6aa-9a45c778361c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a2a87c7-4871-52b2-9751-1dcf545d8473" :answer/id #uuid "4a2a87c7-4871-52b2-9751-1dcf545d8473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c4b18bd-d214-5ab3-980a-bcf8c20a44a8" :answer/id #uuid "9c4b18bd-d214-5ab3-980a-bcf8c20a44a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a192f294-392f-523d-b854-34cf2ca91ca6" :answer/id #uuid "a192f294-392f-523d-b854-34cf2ca91ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-088db5f4-36d3-5c78-98a0-f200bd4afcc7" :answer/id #uuid "088db5f4-36d3-5c78-98a0-f200bd4afcc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-168db077-1d3d-5cb0-b6aa-9a45c778361c" :answer/id #uuid "168db077-1d3d-5cb0-b6aa-9a45c778361c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee5f2c99-4524-5cc2-872a-3bdd6d04d82a" :question/id #uuid "ee5f2c99-4524-5cc2-872a-3bdd6d04d82a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129142" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,2,6)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,4⟩=8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,4⟩ & =8 \\\\ -2x+4y+4z & =8 \\\\ 4z & =8+2x-4y \\\\ z & =2+\\frac{x}{2}-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=2+\\frac{2}{2}-1=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,1,2)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,1,2⟩-⟨-3,2,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-1,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|5\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-4-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{6} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3647b522-cc39-5b80-86fd-13996ce4e48f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3647b522-cc39-5b80-86fd-13996ce4e48f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3647b522-cc39-5b80-86fd-13996ce4e48f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-acf35f72-276b-5ae6-8734-c3d72972ffea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-31b8c44f-f4d9-57d8-90d2-99d7decf9188" "answer-8c1d2c94-d43d-5c24-a663-9d1fbcba711f" "answer-acf35f72-276b-5ae6-8734-c3d72972ffea" "answer-e134b035-3648-5a34-a02a-44af5b1b5f73" "answer-d7d5ba1e-9709-5d81-81a8-a2db338b2a56"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31b8c44f-f4d9-57d8-90d2-99d7decf9188" :answer/id #uuid "31b8c44f-f4d9-57d8-90d2-99d7decf9188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c1d2c94-d43d-5c24-a663-9d1fbcba711f" :answer/id #uuid "8c1d2c94-d43d-5c24-a663-9d1fbcba711f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acf35f72-276b-5ae6-8734-c3d72972ffea" :answer/id #uuid "acf35f72-276b-5ae6-8734-c3d72972ffea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e134b035-3648-5a34-a02a-44af5b1b5f73" :answer/id #uuid "e134b035-3648-5a34-a02a-44af5b1b5f73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7d5ba1e-9709-5d81-81a8-a2db338b2a56" :answer/id #uuid "d7d5ba1e-9709-5d81-81a8-a2db338b2a56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-152abe46-196c-57ed-801a-b01b3b6e9019" :question/id #uuid "152abe46-196c-57ed-801a-b01b3b6e9019" :question/math-academy-id "q-34033" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,0,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $2x-y+2z=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(2)-(3)+2z & =-1 \\\\ 2z & =-2 \\\\ z & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,3,-1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,-1⟩-⟨-1,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨2,-1,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-3\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a75b517-d88b-5fde-8c47-3acf225f13a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a75b517-d88b-5fde-8c47-3acf225f13a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a75b517-d88b-5fde-8c47-3acf225f13a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a40f70a0-ef1e-59d6-9c75-8bb1b576296f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-66952a23-b25c-549f-a606-5d6dda11f34c" "answer-a40f70a0-ef1e-59d6-9c75-8bb1b576296f" "answer-1d85d58b-d2c6-50e6-b647-b9ac50af4bb1" "answer-5ad1e3d5-d1ee-5ca4-bb25-a289369682c6" "answer-75964f2d-1d14-5218-b72a-c985ff68e537"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66952a23-b25c-549f-a606-5d6dda11f34c" :answer/id #uuid "66952a23-b25c-549f-a606-5d6dda11f34c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a40f70a0-ef1e-59d6-9c75-8bb1b576296f" :answer/id #uuid "a40f70a0-ef1e-59d6-9c75-8bb1b576296f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d85d58b-d2c6-50e6-b647-b9ac50af4bb1" :answer/id #uuid "1d85d58b-d2c6-50e6-b647-b9ac50af4bb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ad1e3d5-d1ee-5ca4-bb25-a289369682c6" :answer/id #uuid "5ad1e3d5-d1ee-5ca4-bb25-a289369682c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75964f2d-1d14-5218-b72a-c985ff68e537" :answer/id #uuid "75964f2d-1d14-5218-b72a-c985ff68e537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120020 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
